35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"I found that the covered spaces have been held by the same flats for five years without review. Also, the complaint log shows several disputes over bikes leaning on each other, though no one was held accountable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is quite concerning to hear about those disputes, Misaki. I noticed that the morning rush can be a bit chaotic, with neighbors having to shift other bikes just to leave. It seems a bit stressful for everyone.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Wow, the financial side is a total mystery! The ledger barely covers cleaning and lights, and the treasurer is already spending hours on tiny cash collections. If we add more billing, it'll be a nightmare!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings confirm May's concerns. The treasurer already spends three hours a month on basic reconciliation. Adding per-place billing would only increase this burden, likely leading to the same abandonment we've seen with previous initiatives.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that some of the daily riders would actually prefer to pay a fee rather than just being treated as one equal claim! Also, I saw people having to move other bikes just to get out in the morning!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, @Mio, the fact that people are shifting bikes to leave suggests the current layout is physically inefficient. Combined with the lack of review for five years, it seems we've let a stagnant system create quiet resentment.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, you are quite right. It is a heavy heart that makes me worry; when neighbors must push each other's belongings just to start their day, it can easily lead to frayed nerves and misunderstandings.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, see? I told you the numbers would be interesting! We're basically running on a shoestring budget. If we want any real changes, we can't just wish for them—we'll have to figure out who's actually paying for what!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May, the ""interest"" in the numbers is precisely why we must be cautious. If the treasurer is already struggling with basic tasks, we cannot introduce a complex billing system that requires more hours of labor. It is simply not sustainable.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, @Shizue, it's so frustrating that people have to move other bikes! It's like a puzzle just to leave the house! And @George, if people are actually willing to pay, maybe we can find a way that doesn't make the treasurer's life a nightmare?","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shizue"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, while willingness to pay is helpful, we must be careful. If we implement a system that feels like a transaction or a competition for spots, we risk damaging the social harmony of the building.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I agree. We must be very gentle. I also noticed that some of our neighbors' bicycles are left in the rain, and their saddles stay wet even the next morning. It is quite a pity to start the day that way.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, that does sound miserable! But let's be real—if we want to fix the rain problem or the ""bike puzzle,"" it's going to cost something. We can't just hope for a miracle when the ledger is practically empty!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, cost is not the only factor. We must consider the human cost of administration. If we create a system that requires constant monitoring or complex bookkeeping, it will inevitably collapse once the initial enthusiasm fades.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, I get that, but we can't just do nothing! If people are already grumbling about the same flats always getting the best spots, we have to fix it. Maybe there's a simple way to rotate them without too much paperwork?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, rotation sounds fair in theory, but if not handled carefully, it can create new tensions. We must ensure the solution doesn't turn our lobby into a place where people avoid each other due to parking disputes.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, you have such a thoughtful perspective. I believe that if we can find a way to share the comfort of the eaves and the ease of the morning exit, the harmony will return naturally. Let us be kind to one another.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shizue, kindness is lovely, but it doesn't pay for new racks or a better layout! We're all talking about ""harmony,"" but the real harmony comes from a plan that actually works without bankrupting us or killing the treasurer!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"@May, you are correct that a plan must work. However, a plan that relies on excessive labor is not a working plan. We must prioritize a low-maintenance system that does not depend on a single person's endurance.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@George, I totally agree that we shouldn't burn anyone out! But we can't ignore that the current system is a mess. Let's find a way to be fair and efficient without making it a chore!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
