60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A risks turning our neighbors into competitors, and Option C's rigidity could lead to long-term resentment if some are consistently unlucky. Option B seems the most neutral, as it removes the concept of ""ownership"" entirely.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option B sounds like a wonderful way to let everyone share the space. However, I worry that without a plan, the morning rush might remain a bit chaotic and the rain may still dampen some spirits.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B sounds like a dream for the treasurer, but it's a bit too simple! What about the cost of those double-tier racks? We can't just buy them with hopes and dreams since the ledger is empty!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A is out of the question. Adding monthly charges to the treasurer's already heavy workload is a recipe for failure. We must avoid any system that requires ongoing, tedious bookkeeping and manual reconciliation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@George, I totally agree about the bookkeeping! But @May, if we go with Option B, maybe we can use the money from the daily riders who said they'd pay to buy the racks? It solves the ""bike puzzle"" and the fairness problem all at once!","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""George"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, using a one-time contribution for racks is a practical idea. Option B eliminates the ""ownership"" that causes resentment, which is far better for our long-term social atmosphere than a lottery or a payment system.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, you are so thoughtful. If we can find a way to make the racks easy to use, perhaps the morning shoving matches will stop, and everyone can start their day with a smile and a dry seat.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Mio, that's a clever way to spin it! But let's be honest, getting people to actually hand over cash for a ""contribution"" is just another chore for the treasurer. If we go with B, we need a real budget, not just a wish list!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, you are right. Even ""one-time"" contributions require tracking and collection. Option B is the only choice that removes the administrative burden entirely. It is the only sustainable path that doesn't rely on someone's endless patience.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, you're so right about the sustainability! If we just go with Option B, we don't need to track anything. It's the fastest way to stop the grumbling and make sure no one is stuck in the rain! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, I agree. Option B is the only choice that prevents the building from splitting into ""winners"" and ""losers."" By removing fixed spots, we protect the social fabric of our lobby. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, @Mio, your kindness and logic are very comforting. If we can move away from fixed spots, perhaps we can all be more considerate of one another. I shall vote for Option B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@George, you've practically sold me on it! If it's the only way to keep the treasurer from quitting and avoids a bookkeeping nightmare, I'm in. Let's just hope the racks are actually easy to use! I vote for Option B.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,I agree. Option B is the only rational choice that ensures the system does not collapse under its own administrative weight. It is the only sustainable solution for the long term. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,Yay! I'm so happy we all agree! No more bike puzzles or grumpy faces in the morning. Let's make our parking area the friendliest in the whole neighborhood! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"The consensus is clear. Option B is the most responsible choice, as it prioritizes both administrative sustainability and the social harmony of our residents. I am glad we reached this agreement. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It brings me such peace to see us all in harmony. Let us hope this new arrangement brings a gentle start to everyone's morning and a warm spirit to our building. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Since we're all on the same page, let's just get it done! No more money mysteries or treasurer meltdowns for me. Let's make this work! I vote for Option B.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,"The decision is unanimous and practical. By removing the need for constant oversight and bookkeeping, we ensure the system remains functional without burning anyone out. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we could all agree! It's going to be so much better when everyone can just park and go without any stress. I'm voting for Option B!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
